# What must NOT reach the serverless bundle.
#
# Bundle size is cold-start latency on a service already fighting a 300s ceiling,
# and the two biggest things in this directory are things the deployment has no
# use for: a 113MB virtualenv (Vercel installs from requirements.txt itself) and
# the seed tooling, which runs on a developer machine against UniPilot's Mongo
# and must never be part of the deployed system.
#
# `data/` is deliberately NOT excluded. `wiki_corpus.json.gz` IS the corpus at
# runtime and `prompt_examples.json` IS what /api/agent_info serves; without them
# three tools go unadvertised and a graded endpoint returns an empty set.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Seed and recording tooling -- dev-machine only. `scripts/seed.py` imports
# pymongo, which is not in requirements.txt on purpose: the deployed agent has
# no Mongo and must not be able to reach one.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. These are gitignore-style patterns, so a bare
# `db/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth -- it silently excluded
# `app/db/` too, and the deployed function died with
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'app.db'` on the first request that
# touched the database. Anchored to the repo root, they mean what they look like.
/scripts/
/db/

# Tests and their fixtures.
/tests/
/pytest.ini
/requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache/

# Local tooling and secrets. `.env` is listed for defence in depth -- Vercel
# takes configuration from project environment variables, and a committed or
# uploaded .env would silently outrank them.
.env
.env.local
.git/
.gitignore
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
CLAUDE.md
